WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:02.548
(soft music)

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:10.506
- [The Sanctuary Tree]
Deet, All Thra is at risk.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.300
The darkening corrupts
everything it touches.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.540
- What is the The Darkening?

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.047
- [The Sanctuary Tree] Behold.

00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:23.570
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.390
- It was so exciting for us as a company,

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.130
also as a family to get to come back

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.477
to the world of "The Dark Crystal."

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:37.110
It was such a beautifully
realized whole universe

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.700
between all original creations,
all original characters.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.600
For us to be able to re-create that world

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.470
and expand upon it and
make it sort of bigger,

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.970
more ambitious even
than the original film,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:53.010
this has really been
one of the most amazing

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.260
projects we've ever done.

00:00:57.105 --> 00:01:00.070
There's so much handcraft
in "The Dark Crystal"

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.300
that we really wanted to show people

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.660
some of these things up close.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.210
So when you come to the exhibition

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.380
you're seeing the actual puppets,

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.850
actual props and you can
see how handmade it is

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.700
which makes it so very different from CG

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.650
and then of course when you see the show

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.160
you see that the puppets
are brought to life

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.430
by individual puppeteers.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.120
It's really a very different art form

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.440
than animation and than CG.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.610
We want people to be able
to come to the exhibit

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.100
and just actually see
what it all looks like

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.530
up close because up close you almost can't

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:34.480
believe the detail.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.610
This is funny don't feed him.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:37.728
Anyway

00:01:37.728 --> 00:01:40.645
(mysterious music)

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.730
We're so excited that
the show uses puppetry.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.820
This is what people love
about "The Dark Crystal".

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.980
Of course, we wanted to
do the "Age of Resistance"

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.100
with puppets as well.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.040
Most of the puppetry is pretty
much the same techniques

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:55.873
as in the original.

00:01:55.873 --> 00:02:00.240
In some cases we just
moved the materials along

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.920
to a level so that the
puppets would just work

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:04.180
a little bit better.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.160
Some of the foam that's
done and used is more

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.180
expressive so the Gelfing
have a little more

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.310
expression in their face.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.850
But, this is a basic
kind of animatronic setup

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.080
of one of our characters, the Pluffm.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.710
He's radio-controlled.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.930
You know, my father started
using radio controls

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.020
in the 70's.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.263
We're still using that same technology.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.940
We were so lucky that Netflix commissioned

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.990
a feature-length
documentary about the making

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:28.823
of this series and sometimes

00:02:28.823 --> 00:02:32.040
you just wanna see what the puppeteers do.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.060
It's real physical labor.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.600
They are at the absolute
top of their art form

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.940
and it's something that very few people

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.580
in the world know how
to do but these are the

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.430
very best in the world.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.400
At the same time, we're bringing in CG

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.230
just to enhance a little
bit but most of what

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.490
we're using CG for is to enhance the world

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:57.130
so we have big sets where we
made them much, much bigger

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.833
and we make the world much
more expansive through CG.

00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:03.700
(archaic Chinese music)

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.690
These are some really beautiful props.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.210
This is Brea's journal.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.450
Her little paints and paint brush.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.730
And this is the Skeksis Book of Law

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.490
which is one of our
hero props in the show.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.830
There was a whole kind
of art department side

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.780
to this that was really
special and they kind of worked

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.250
off to the side.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.428
We were always kind of in
awe of what they were doing.

00:03:26.428 --> 00:03:29.261
(inspiring music)

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.700
So this is the Chamberlain,
he's one of the main characters,

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.450
who's one of everybody's favorites

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.713
because he has such a distinctive voice.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.520
- [Chamberlain] You must be careful!

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.400
I may not always be here to save you.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.570
- [Lisa] All of this food is so weird

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.400
and it looks even stranger on screen.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.960
They eat like things that are actually,

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.730
still appear to be living,

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.130
like the tentacles would be moving.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:01.030
The banquet scene is such
a favorite in the film.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.030
Everybody remembers that
scene cause it was so gross

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.900
and we wanted to make
sure our banquet scene

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.773
was really gross as well.

00:04:11.707 --> 00:04:15.040
(archaic Chinese music)

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.210
Coming here is a great opportunity to see

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.970
how beautiful the costumes are up close

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.610
because the amount of handwork

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.320
on these costumes is extraordinary.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.320
It's like the kind of work
that goes into period costumes

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.370
and people get very
excited if they see a show

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.030
that takes place in the 18th century.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:41.490
But, the same amount of work is in these

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.440
small costumes and
they're really incredible.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:45.323
- Join me!

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.230
So we may finally unite as one

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.467
against our true foe, the Skeksis.

00:04:51.487 --> 00:04:54.034
- [Emperor] We are eternal!

00:04:54.034 --> 00:04:55.610
(dramatic music playing)

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.160
- [Hannah] We're at the BFI Southbank

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.904
and we're about to watch the premiere

00:04:58.904 --> 00:05:00.560
of "The Dark Crystal:
the Age of Resistance",

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.710
and it feels freaking awesome.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.290
- [Brian] It's really exciting because

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.387
we started this project,
what, 40 years ago?

00:05:07.387 --> 00:05:08.940
- Almost 40 years ago

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.000
And here we are.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.150
And it's bigger and
better than it ever was.

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.180
(dramatic music)

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:17.150
- [Louis] It's so different from anything

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.020
you've seen before.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.170
I mean, you've seen "The Dark Crystal,"

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.003
the original movie.

00:05:20.003 --> 00:05:21.910
But there's nothing that looks like this.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.470
You know, and it's really
thanks to these people

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:24.303
can you focus?

00:05:24.303 --> 00:05:27.050
These people are the real
champions of this movie.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.170
They are the puppeteers.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:31.860
- As wonderful as it is, CGI
and all this new technology,

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:33.980
it's just so nice to
kind of have a fantasy

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.022
told by puppets.

00:05:36.022 --> 00:05:39.908
- [The Myth Speaker]
Who catches the light,

00:05:39.908 --> 00:05:41.825
stares in the darkness.

00:05:43.383 --> 00:05:44.876
Revealing

00:05:44.876 --> 00:05:46.328
your destiny.

00:05:46.328 --> 00:05:49.745
(dramatic music playing)

